A||N||4||nlschmidt||manifold gaskets for a v6||||1||
Z||000000||nlschmidt||03-18-2000||05:29 PM||||I think fieros are great ,I did at one time own 6 of them. I plan on rebulding my v6 in my 87 GT Fastback and heard that there is suppose to be a copper impregnated gasket made for the exhaust manifold, which is not supposed to blow out like the original ones do.knowing it,s not fun changing these I was hoping someone could help me out with the problem.  THANK YOU Mr, Lynn Schmidt||||reg||1
Z||000001||Eric||03-18-2000||06:19 PM||||I used Felpro and I've yet to hear anybody having a problem with the exhaust manifold gaskets.  Remember to grind out the restrictions while you have them off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WisconsinGT||03-18-2000||06:51 PM||||While we are on the topic of gaskets....I found out the other day that I have an exhaust leak at the base of my EGR valve. The gasket bit the dust. So I thought I might be able to do this myself. Anyway, can I change the gasket by taking out the two bolts that hold the EGR valve. Or should I also take out the two bolts that connect the EGR tube as well? Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||03-19-2000||02:49 AM||||Best to remove the EGR tube since the bolts that hold the EGR valve on are quite long and if the gasket just under the valve went, then the one under the spacer isn't far behind and since you will have it apart it would be best to do it all at once.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||03-19-2000||09:50 AM||||mshill thanks for the info. I was wondering about the other gasket above the basw EGR gasket. Are they both the same type of gasket? I guess I better get another. Thanks||||reg||1
